---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import Compare from "../components/Compare.astro";
import { neighbors } from "../lib/nav";
const { prev, next } = neighbors("inheritance");
---

<Base title="10. Inheritance & polymorphism — C# vs TypeScript" description="10. Inheritance & polymorphism: side-by-side C# and TypeScript examples." slug="inheritance">
  <div slot="header" id="top">
    <p><small><a href="/">C# vs TS</a> / 10. Inheritance & polymorphism</small></p>
    <h1>10. Inheritance &amp; polymorphism</h1>
    <p><strong>How to read:</strong> left is C#, middle is TypeScript, right is blank Mystery (yours). Narrow screens stack.</p>
  </div>

  <section id="inheritance">
  
  <h2>10. Inheritance &amp; polymorphism</h2>
  <Compare>
    <div slot="left">
      <pre><code>public abstract class Animal
&#123;
  public abstract string Speak();
  public virtual string Move() =&gt; "walks";
&#125;
public sealed class Dog : Animal
&#123;
  public override string Speak() =&gt; "woof";
  public override string Move() =&gt; "runs";
&#125;
Animal a = new Dog();
Console.WriteLine(a.Speak()); // woof</code></pre>
    </div>
    <div slot="right">
      <pre><code>export abstract class Animal &#123;
  abstract speak(): string;
  move(): string &#123; return "walks"; &#125;
&#125;
export class Dog extends Animal &#123;
  override speak(): string &#123; return "woof"; &#125;
  override move(): string &#123; return "runs"; &#125;
&#125;
const a: Animal = new Dog();
console.log(a.speak()); // woof</code></pre>
    </div>
  </Compare>
  <ul>
    <li><code>abstract → abstract</code>, <code>virtual → plain</code>, <code>override → override</code>, <code>sealed →</code> no keyword (don’t extend / lint rule).</li>
    <li>Both: single class inheritance + multiple interfaces. TS adds mixins via intersection + helper functions.</li>
  </ul>

  </section>

  <nav class="pager" aria-label="Previous / next topic">
    <span>{prev ? <a href={`/${prev.slug}/`}>← {prev.title}</a> : <span />}</span>
    <span><a href="/">All topics</a></span>
    <span>{next ? <a href={`/${next.slug}/`}>{next.title} →</a> : <span />}</span>
  </nav>
</Base>
